Package: OptSurvCutR
Type: Package
Title: Optimal Survival Cut-point Discovery for Time-to-Event Analysis
Version: 0.1.7
Date: 2025-10-25
Author: Payton Yau [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Payton Yau <tungon@gmail.com>
Description:
    Provides a comprehensive workflow to determine, find, and
    validate optimal cut-points for continuous predictors in a survival
    (time-to-event) context. The package includes functions to first
    determine the optimal number of cut-point(s), then find their
    location(s) using either a systematic search, a genetic algorithm, or a
    spline-based method for U-shaped relationships. It can also assess
    the stability of the result via bootstrapping. The methods are described
    in Yau, Payton T.O. (2025) doi:10.1101/2025.10.08.681246.
